Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
we're joined now by stephanie  rawlings-blake if her name and her face  sounds familiar it's because she's used  to dealing with tragedy and controversy  she's a former mayor of baltimore she's  now serving as travis scott's  spokesperson stephanie it's good to see  you i'm very sorry it's under these  circumstances this story is  heartbreaking on so many different  levels you know there's a lot of finger  pointing going on much of it directed to  travis scott in particular from some of  the people who were there that night can  you tell us when was he aware that this  concert had turned into such a tragedy  so first thank you for uh having me and  it it is sorry that it's under these  circumstances um yeah there's a lot of  confusion as you saw in the clip  proceeding it was chaotic and  just like the police officers who were  standing  in front of the stage with travis nearly  30 minutes after it was declared a  public safety emergency travis had no  idea what was going on until well later  hours and hours later  how was he notified  he was notified by his team  after the event after he was already  gone from the event as you saw there was  so much chaos so much breakdown uh in  the communication and that's why it was  important for me uh to to work to try to  help him out nine people have lost their  lives nine families are grieving and and  gail i'm a mom my daughter's gone to one  of these big concerts and i can tell you  i spent three sleepless nights every day  watching my phone watching her location  because when you have crowds of 50 000  people anything can happen and while a  lot of people are trying to place the  blame travis is taking responsibility  for moving forward and trying to make  sure this never happens again to  anyone's child  yeah there are reports that he had gone  to dave and busters and was partying i  think it's important to point out that  when he was at dave and busters he  couldn't possibly have known that this  was that this had  devolved into what it had become  no absolutely not he was there trying to  regroup with his team  they were trying to figure out what was  going on it was hours and hours after  the concert when they actually found out  the tragedy how the tragedy unfolded and  he has not stopped grieving for these  families he knows that he is who he is  because of his fans his love for his  fans is so deep i was struck when i was  speaking to him how deeply he was  hurting because of what happened to  the people he loves and in the city that  he loves  yeah i heard you say that he's taken  responsibility what do you mean by that  and he wants to make sure this doesn't  happen again what do you mean  when i say responsibility someone has to  say  where are the breakdowns where was the  communication breakdown where was the  public safety breakdown i mean this  notion that travis had the ability to  stop the concert is ludicrous they have  a 59  page operations plan and it clearly says  the only two people that are  have the authority to stop the concert  where the executive producer and the  concert producer  he was not responsible for this but he  wants to be responsible for the solution  and i'm here to make sure that we can  connect the dots and to make sure that  this tragedy that there's a lesson out  of this tragedy and something like this  doesn't happen again  you know you pointed out there is video  of police officers in front of the stage  they actually seem to be enjoying the  concert they were seem to be singing  along and videotaping  and they're right in front of travis at  the time so they didn't appear to be  aware of it certainly travis didn't  appear to be aware of it did travis  scott and your and his team have any  conversations with officials before  about safety at this event  yes his team is always concerned about  safety um you know he does not hide from  the fact that in the past he has made  mistakes but one thing he said to me and  he looked me in his uh in my eyes and  said that he's learned from that and  that's why he takes safety so  seriously he stopped when he saw that  some he saw that something was a myth he  couldn't tell what it was but he's so  concerned about his fans he stopped you  in the video show he stopped multiple  times to try to get a sense of what was  going on and just like those police  officers that were standing in front of  the stage he could not tell what was  going on  has he reached out to any of the  families stephanie  oh absolutely  first i want to say that we're  respectful he's very respectful of their  their need for privacy and space as they  grieve but he's reached out to all of  the families  i've reached out to  the latest  unfortunate victim to let them know that  in their time  um he's there he's here to help if they  want hit  all right stephanie rawlings-blake thank  you for taking the time to speak with us  this morning thank you my pleasure

